[[2047,127,0,"<aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Before\nremoving and refitting the control unit, carry out the following\npreliminary operations:Place the ignition key\nin the OFF position and extract it;Disconnect\nthe battery leads and insulate.Wait for 10\nminutes before continuing.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>FOLLOW ALL THE RECOMMENDED SAFETY\nRULES (\n                                                         <a href=\"#/3238524\">5580C</a>\n                                                          - Precautions).</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3238803\">7040A65</a>\n                                           (Right side)</p><p><strong>- 5010B44 rear seat air duct - arrange</strong>\n                                           (Right\nside)</p><p>1. Rotate the safety bracket (1a) in the direction of the arrow\nand disconnect the electrical connection (1b).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Air bag control unit</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236934\">M60</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Unscrew the bolts</p><p>3. Remove the control unit.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018891.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Follow these precautions:</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>never strike or shake the control\nunit; do not connect the electrical connection to the control unit before\nhaving fixed the control unit correctly; Make sure that the battery\nis disconnected.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>If the control unit is being replaced,\nremove the removable part of the adhesive label from the new control\nunit and place it in a special file containing the vehicle details\n(model, registration date, chassis number) and the serial number\nof the old control unit. This file should be kept for future checks.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>1. Position the control unit (1a).</p><p>Make sure that the arrow (1b) on the upper surface of the control\nunit is pointing in the direction of travel.</p><p>2. Tighten the bolts to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>AIR BAG CONTROL UNIT</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.8</p></td></tr></table></div><p>3. Connect the electrical connection (3a) and secure it by rotating\nthe safety bracket (3b) in the direction of the arrow.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018892.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,96,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Follow these precautions:</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Before\nremoving and refitting the control unit, carry out the following\npreliminary operations.Place the ignition key\nin the OFF position and extract it;Disconnect\nthe battery leads and insulate.Wait for 10\nminutes before continuing.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>FOLLOW ALL THE RECOMMENDED SAFETY\nRULES (\n                                                               <a href=\"#/3238524\">5580C</a>\n                                                                - Precautions).</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p><a href=\"#/3238803\">7040A65</a>\n                                           (left\nand right sides)</p><p>1. Disconnect electrical connections (1a), (1b).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1a</p></td><td><p>Air bag control unit</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236938\">M60B</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Air bag control unit</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236935\">M60A</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Unscrew the bolts</p><p>3. Remove the control unit.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018893.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,96,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Follow these precautions:</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>never strike or shake the control\nunit; do not connect the electrical connection to the control unit before\nhaving fixed the control unit correctly; Make sure that the battery\nis disconnected.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>If the control unit is being replaced,\nremove the removable part of the adhesive label from the new control\nunit and place it in a special file containing the vehicle details\n(model, registration date, chassis number) and the serial number\nof the old control unit. This file should be kept for future checks.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>1. Position the control unit (1a). Make sure that the arrow (1b)\non the upper surface of the control unit is pointing in the direction\nof travel.</p><p>2. Tighten the bolts to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>